\par\par \b \uc2  Czech crown eases, bonds down but in tight range. \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1999\par 10:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0800 GMT - Czech crown eases, slightly influenced by Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown, but lacking other impulses, still maintains the trend from previous days. Bonds moderately lower. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Crown\tab   at 37.676/696 from about 37.600 at the open and 37.605/635 late on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two waves to support its crown on Monday, buying 30 million euros worth of crowns after a large corporate order of a similar amount had pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply lower. \par \par \uc2  * "It (Czech crown) started easing yesterday evening slightly (in reaction to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown), which may also be a reason for today's easing," said Lucie Rubesova, a dealer at Bank Austria Creditanstalt. \par \par \uc2  "The crown has been in the range of between 37.55 and 37.70 for a couple of days, until a new impuls comes, it should remain in this range," Rubesova said. \par \par \uc2  * Crown seen in range between 37.55 and 37.70 during the day. \par \par \uc2  * Czech bonds lower. The state benchmark 10.90/3 at 111.35/112.65, yielding 7.62/7.54 from 111.55/85 at the open. The 14.85/3 at 122.60/90, yielding 7.59/7.51 from 122.80/10. \par \par \uc2  ((Klara Gajduskova, Prague newsroom, +420-2-2423-0003, fax +420-2-2422-9935, prague.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5i00ws6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\pic