\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  in thrall to FOMC. \b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1999\par 12:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 18 (Reuters) - The dramatic Labour Party victory in Israel was overshadowed on Tuesday by the meeting later in the day of the Federal Open Markets Committee and the shekel firmed only slightly. \par \par \uc2  By 0950 GMT, the Isreali \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 4.071 to the dollar, up from Monday's close in London of 4.105. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and strategists were still divided on whether the Fed would signal it is willing to tighten monetary policy in the wake of a surprising 0.7 percent jump in the U.S. Consumer Price Index for April. \par \par \uc2  Any tightening by the Fed would have a follow-through impact on the monetary policy of countries most closely tied to the U.S., such as Singapore, where the dollar firmed against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 1.710 from a previous close of 1.715. \par \par \uc2  "Meanwhile, Singapore interest rates remain focused on the outcome of the FOMC meeting tonight. This will have an impact in a domestic market already worried that the stronger-than-expected U.S. inflation data for April will see a similar result in Singapore inflation for April which may turn positive when it is released next Monday," said Mitul Kotecha, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist as Standard Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Kotecha is expecting a tightening bias at the Fed. \par \par \uc2  Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also firmer, with the Indonesian rupiah rising to 7,850 to the dollar from 7,950 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In emerging Europe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded sideways to slightly weaker, awaiting the Fed. \par \par \uc2  Mark Rall, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank, believes there is only a 40 percent chance of a tightening bias at the Fed. He said sentiment towards \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region should focus on domestic factors. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak crown continued weaker on Tuesday in the wake of a surprisingly strong showing of former premier Vladimir Meciar in presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  Despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to weaken and was trading 46.674/874 against the euro in London trade. \par \par \uc2  "We think that although there is a high probability that (Rudolf) Schuster will win the second round of the presidential election, the fact that Meciar's position is still very strong worries investors," said Rall. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     37.66   37.62   0.11%   8.23%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab   4.18    4.18    0.01%   2.78%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab  250.17  250.06  0.04%   -0.41%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 46.69   46.42   0.57%   8.57%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab  15,400  15,255  0.95%   40.64%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab  3.99    3.92    1.74%   1.53%\par South Africa\tab \tab   6.15    6.19    -0.60%  5.25%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    69.05   68.65   0.58%   12.09%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.080   4.105   -0.62%  -0.95%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab   9.31    9.31    0.00%   -5.39%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab   1.6660  1.6660  0.00%   38.02%\par Venezuela\tab \tab      594.50  594.50  0.00%   5.31%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab    487.00  487.00  0.00%   3.57%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore\tab \tab      1.710   1.715   -0.29%  3.26%\par H