\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak c.bank says client payments weakened crown. \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 1999\par 16:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, May 17 (Reuters) - The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters on Monday that the weakening of the crown which caused it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been based on client payments. \par \par \uc2  "According to our latest information it was all to do with client payments in commercial banks," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Jan Onda said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least twice to defend the crown on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, the first time at around 46.700 to the euro and the second time at 46.300, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Onda said he could not reveal the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had used during its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1353 GMT the crown was quoted at 46.448/548 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters earlier that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been in line with established policy of moving against sharp fluctuations but not in favour of any specific rate. ((Robin Shepherd, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5h00loa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
