\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak cbank says money market moves more likely. \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 1999\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, May 13 (Reuters) - The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters on Thursday that any moves to influence the rate of the crown were more likely on the money markets than through direct foreign exhange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "What room there is for monetary policy, we see in the area of crown activities rather than in direct foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Masar said in an interview. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown, which was floated in October last year, has been touching all time low levels against the euro in recent days. In early afternoon trading it was quoted at 45.45/55 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier that its decision not to add liquidity to the money market on Thursday was partly because of recent developments in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  However, shortly after announcing there would be no repo, what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called an "extreme" reaction on the markets sent overnight rates soaring to around 17 percent from 10 percent. The bank then set an overnight repo to calm the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have been slowly falling in recent weeks. As of May 5, they stood at $2.7 billion. ((Robin Shepherd, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5d015ly\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngb