\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak c.bank says crown reflects fundamentals. \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 1999\par 12:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, April 22 (Reuters) - Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Vladimir Masar said on Thursday that recent depreciation of the Slovak crown was a reflection of developments in the deficits of Slovak public finances and foreign trade. \par \par \uc2  "It is true that some depreciation has been taking place in the Slovak crown lately," Masar told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "Exchange rate changes reflect the status of solving or not solving macro economic problems: development of public finances and of foreign trade...I have to still say that we unfortunately haven't recorded a reversal in the development of these two indicators," he said. \par \par \uc2  Masar said the Slovak crown had weakened four percent against the euro, the reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since the beginning of the year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to set a specific crown rate, but may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against high volatility not based on economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The crown was quoted at 44.89/97 to the euro at 1025 GMT, unchanged from earlier. ((Andrej Salner, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4m02lbe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
