\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says no need to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  at present. \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 13:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, March 10 (Reuters) - The director of the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  asset department told Reuters on Wednesday that the bank saw no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the crown at current levels. \par \par \uc2  "At the current level, we don't see any need to enter this market. The situation is calmer than it was yesterday," Frantisek Szulenyi said. \par \par \uc2  At the time of Szulenyi's comments the crown was quoted at 44.45/54 to the euro from 44.50/60 at the open. \par \par \uc2  Volatility began to shake the market on Tuesday morning, caused, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, by a marked decline in short term interbank interest rates itself brought on by a liquidity surplus. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded directly by buying crowns. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly by selling short term T-bills from its portfolio to slected banks and then on Wednesday through a repo tender to drain liquidity. All three measures were the first of their kind on the Slovak market since the crown was floated on October 1, last year. \par \par \uc2  Interest rates on the Slovak money market ranged from 9/10 bid/offer on overnights to 15.5/16.5 quoted for six month funds. On Tuesday, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, they were quoted at between 4.0 and 16.0 percent, for maturities from overnights to six months. \par \par \uc2  Szulenyi said the stabilisation of the crown had been helped by the rise in interest rates, especially short term maturities. \par \par \uc2  ((Robin Shepherd, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv3a05of4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
