\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  on crown if needed-paper. \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 1998\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said it was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to either support or weaken the crown but did not reveal at what level, the Narodna Obroda daily said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  It quoted the National Bank of Slovakia's director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  asset management, Frantisek Szulenyi, as saying that the bank wanted to see the crown stabilised after its flotation on October 1. \par \par \uc2  "The NBS again confirmed its interest in the fastest possible stabilisation of the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and declared that if it considers its exchange rate under or overvalued, it is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the paper quoted Szulenyi as saying. \par \par \uc2  "We also stressed that an acceptable way of doing this is through a selected brokerage and five to six selected commercial banks," he said. The paper said Szulenyi spoke at a meeting of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  representatives with selected banks on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Szulenyi did not say at what levels the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  nor at what levels it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolished the crown's plus/minus 7.0 percent band around a mark-dollar basket on October 1 after investors speculating on a devaluation sent the crown sharply lower and forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The crown dropped sharply after the flotation but has since regained some ground and has stabilised at around 12 percent below the central parity of the former basket. Pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was caused by high foreign trade and budget deficits and mounted after a general election in late September. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the flotation. \par \par \uc2  The crown was quoted at 21.95/15 to the mark at 0810 GMT on Thursday, about 12 percent under the midpoint of its former basket. \par \par \uc2  ((Jan Lopatka, Bratislava Newsroom,421-7-521, fax 421-7-521-8402 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duaf01x9e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
