\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak National Bank Announces Supervised  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Float \b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 1998\par 17:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA -(Dow Jones)- The National Bank of Slovakia intends to pursue a policy of allowing the Slovak koruna to trade in a "supervised float," according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Marian Jusko. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a press briefing Monday following a meeting between opposition party economists and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, Jusko said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to assist the koruna if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't happy with trading. \par \par \uc2  "If the float moves in an undesired direction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said, but offered few additional specifics. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  koruna is only in its second full day under its new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday removed the fluctuation band used to guide the koruna since 1993 and let the koruna float against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329dua501b9y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
