\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak Natl Bank/Reserves -2: Chooses Mark As Key  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 1998\par 15:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of Slovakia is satisfied with its current level of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and has no plans to try and boost its holdings, Friday said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Marian Jusko. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a press conference in Bratislava, Jusko said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has access to foreign reserves via international banking sources, but that it sees no need at present to seek additional funding. \par \par \uc2  Jusko said he and others at the bank are satisfied with trading in the first day with neither band nor basket guiding the market. On Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  removed a fluctuation band and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket used to guide the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1993, and allowed the Slovak koruna to freely float. It wasn't necessary for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, Jusko said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  koruna (SKK) immediately devalued by more than 6% against the dollar and the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  The change in monetary policy followed weeks of speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forced to allow the koruna to weaken due in part to a current account deficit of 11% of gross domestic product and rising levels of external debt. \par \par \uc2  Jusko didn't comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has any desired level at which it wants to see the koruna trading, but he did say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will follow the Deutsche mark as its key \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , until 1999, when it will switch to the euro as its main \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  koruna, it isn't planning to extensively manage the koruna's developments, he said. \par \par \uc2  Inflation, which is always a byproduct of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation, isn't seen as a serious problem in 1999, he said, but he didn't give any specifics. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 02-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1353GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020227dua2002jg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
