\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown firms vs basket on Czech crown rally. \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1998\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, July 2 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown extended its gains against the mark/dollar basket in early Thursday activity, boosted again by a Czech crown firming against the mark. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT, the Slovak crown was quoted at 35.090/140 to the dollar and at 19.300/330 to the mark, 2.30 percent on the depreciation side of the basket. It opened at minus 2.45 percent against the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak crown has gained around 75 basis points against the basket since Tuesday, spurred by bullish sentiment on other European emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  "It is clear that today's move came through the Czech crown, though there were no big volumes traded with the Slovak (crown) so far," said Martin Macko, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Istrobanka. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown broke through the key 18/mark level in early Thursday trading, with dealers predicting a further firming of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It all now depends on the Czech/mark development and the market is eying the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as there are fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Macko added. \par \par \uc2  However, traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown should not firm through a level of minus 2.0 percent in the near future. \par \par \uc2  Money market rates were stable at around 11 percent for overnights and 12 percent for one months. ((Peter Laca, Bratislava Newsroom, +421-7-521-8402, fax +421-7-521-8403, bratislava.newroom@reuters.com). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7201m95\par }\page {\par\fs20{