\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  - Czech recoils,  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  skids. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mike Dolan \par \uc2 892 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 15:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted the Czech crown to recoil on Tuesday from its highest level against the German mark since last May's devaluation. \par \par \uc2  The neighbouring Slovak crown skidded too after the Republic of Slovakia's credit rating was downgraded to below investment grade by Moody's Investors Service late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, a benign international investment environment persisted, with investors still happy to take on risky assets in return for high yields. Even the steep rise of the British pound this week is testament to this hunger for yield, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The continued calm helped the Romanian leu weather Monday's resignation of Prime Minister Victor Ciorbea. \par \par \uc2  Ukraine's hryvnia was also little changed as Sunday's elections showed a swing to the left as the Communists took a quarter of party-list seats with half the vote counted. \par \par \uc2  "The recent carefree market sentiment seems to be broadly intact, but there are some signs of consolidation and profit-taking and market rallies in Asia have topped out," said one trader at a UK bank. \par \par \uc2  Broad-based dollar strength also pushed the South African rand weaker in the wake of Monday's drop through the psychologically-important 5-per-dollar level. \par \par \uc2  But central Europe remained the centre of attention, helped by the lure of long-term convergence plays as European Union accession talks started with six countries - Poland, Czech Republic, Hungary, Slovenia, Estonia and Cyprus. \par \par \uc2  Before the Czech National Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, the crown had surged to test as high as 18.25 per mark - its strongest level since it was freely floated last May. \par \par \uc2  "They are squeezing domestic demand by keeping interest rates high and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking the heat in a market that seems to be happy to pick up yield anywhere," said Andrew Kenningham, east European fixed income analyst at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  "There might be some concern it is back to last May's level but the Czech Republic is in a better position fiscally and in terms of its balance of payments than it was last year." \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said further crown strength was likely to be resisted by more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even if the extent and the timing of crown sales will now be very important. \par \par \uc2  "The way the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responds to further crown strength is now critical," said a senior research analyst at another U.S. investment bank. \par \par \uc2  "It (CNB) could have a bit of a policy dilemma if forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily, as this would increase domestic liquidity at a time they are trying to keep things tight to rein in inflation." \par \par \uc2  Earlier the Slovak crown weakened to as low as 3.0 percent below its parity against a basket of officially-targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , versus 1.70 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Moody's downgraded the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt to Ba1, one notch below investment grade. The crown recovered slightly later to trade about 2.60 percent below. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a tight grip on the market, ratings downgrades would further deter foreign direct and portfolio investments needed to bridge the country's current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  Concern about the country's ability to finance itself is also a worry because some existing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowings are directly linked to credit ratings. A $200 million sovereign loan made earlier this year, for example, triggers optional redemptions if the ratings fall to the equivalent of Ba3. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Polish zloty held firm at just under 7.0 percent stronger than its basket parity, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not required to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second consecutive day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Asia, the Thai baht underperformed after Moody's said it lowered the financial strength ratings of five Thai banks. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKETS SNAPSHOT The following is a snapshot of emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. ASIA    * Indonesian rupiah\tab   8,450 per dollar bid vs 8,600 late in London on Monday. * Malaysian ringgit\tab   at 3.625 per dollar from 3.63 per dollar. Thai baht\tab     38.80 per dollar vs 38.00. Philippine peso\tab   37.70 per dollar vs 37.30. * South Korean won     1,384 versus 1,382. * Singapore dollar\tab   1.612 per dollar versus 1.6065. Taiwan dollar\tab   at 32.80 vs 32.805.\par    * Indian rupee\tab     at 39.40 per dollar vs 39.45.\par    EUROPE\tab \tab \par    * Russian rouble\tab     at 6.0975 per dollar bid vs 6.0880.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's daily bid/offer rates at 6.0890/6.1270\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  versus 6.0880/6.1240.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    * Zloty about 6.80 percent above basket parity from 6.81/79\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  percent at the open. Mark/Czech crown\tab \tab  at 18.458 bid\par \f28 \par \p