\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak Koruna Falls Vs Basket In Echo Of Czech Koruna \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par 16:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--Tremors from the Czech Republic continued to rock the Slovak koruna Tuesday, with the Slovakian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen weakening against its fixing basket in highly illiquid, erratic trading. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday the koruna was seen trading on the weak side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  National Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, which allows the koruna to trade within a range of plus or minus 7% from the midpoint, against a basket of 60% Deutsche mark and 40% dollar. \par \par \uc2  'The range of bid prices is 1% to 7% on the weak side of the band,' said Tibor Fratrik, chief dealer at ING Bank in Bratislava. 'There's no liquidity. You can't really predict what will happen on this market more than three hours in the future.' \par \par \uc2  At 1327 GMT traders quoted the dollar at around 34.635 koruna. They quoted the mark at 20.800 koruna, in trading seen tightly focused on the Czech market, which has been rocked by speculation against the Czech koruna. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday afternoon that the bank's monetary policy 'remains stable' and hasn't changed. \par \par \uc2  That's in stark contrast to the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which announced abruptly late Monday that it would discontinue its own \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to let the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely with a peg against the mark. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1430GMT 