\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-SLOVAK C.BANK SIGNALS SUPPORT FOR CROWN. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Laca \par \uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, May 15 (Reuter) - The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) sent a strong signal on Thursday that it would support the Slovak crown to prevent turmoil on the Czech market from pulling the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down. \par \par \uc2  NBS Treasury Director Frantisek Szulenyi told Reuters the Slovak crown was under control at the moment, but added the bank was ready to "react quickly and support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if neccessary". \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hit by what dealers said were massive sales of Slovak crowns resulting from the fall of the Czech crown earlier in the day. The Slovak crown lost some 45 basis points as about $100 million left the country. \par \par \uc2  "This (statement) really showed a new direction and helped to calm down the market," said Dusan Svitek, an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the largest Slovak market player, Slovenska Sporitelna. \par \par \uc2  Svitek said the crown strengthened by around 25 basis points after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comment and moved to around -0.50 percent versus its mark/dollar basket parity. \par \par \uc2  "Though further development will still much depend on the Czech crown moves, I see the Slovak crown ranging between parity and one percent in the depreciation sphere, a point at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown is closely related to the Czech crown since foreign banks often play the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  together so the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually move in tandem. \par \par \uc2  The Czech and Slovak republics used to be united in the Czechoslovak federation which split peacefully in 1993 and the two economies are still very closely linked. \par \par \uc2  Svitek noted that the NBS sent also a second, indirect, signal to the market through its fixing on Thursday, indicating it would not let the Slovak crown fall too far. \par \par \uc2  The NBS on Thursday fixed the crown at 32.990 to the dollar and at 19.542 to the mark, implying a deviation of -0.25 percent versus the basket midpoint. \par \par \uc2  The crown was trading at -0.61 percent at the time of the fixing calculation. \par \par \uc2  Tibor Fratrik, a dealer at ING Bank, said he saw the run on the Slovak crown earlier on Thursday as pure speculation and not based on fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "I would say it was just bargain hunting, in which also some domestic banks were involved," he said. "This decline (of the Slovak crown) seems to me a short-term phenomena which will not set a longer-term trend." \par \par \uc2  Fratrik said he expected the crown to move between parity and -0.1 percent versus the midpoint and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared content for it to stay within this range. \par \par \uc2  -- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130dt5f015dj\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*